> > > I wanted to follow up with this. I have adjusted my code slightly to include starting values, increase maxit control, and use the Nelder-Mead method to avoid calculating the Hessian matrix. I no longer receive NaNs but I still have separation in my models, which I accounted for with penalized likelihood (essentially the same process as before but with a few extra steps). Unfortunately, I have fewer significant results with this code, but I believe it to be more robust than what I had initially developed. However, I am still not certain if this approach is valid or if I need to use a space-for-time substitution to account for the missing repeat surveys. Any recommendations?
> > >
